DAY 39 - PART A: THEORY
kubeadm Part 2: init, join, Certificates, kubeconfig
Time: 30-40 minutes
==================================================================

1. WHAT "kubeadm init" DOES (PHASES)
------------------------------------
  preflight           checks (what you ran yesterday)
  certs               creates the CA and all certs in /etc/kubernetes/pki
  kubeconfig          admin.conf, kubelet.conf, controller-manager.conf,
                      scheduler.conf, super-admin.conf
  kubelet-start       writes kubelet config, starts kubelet
  control-plane       writes static pod manifests (apiserver,
                      controller-manager, scheduler)
  etcd                writes etcd static pod manifest
  wait-control-plane  waits until the API answers
  upload-config       stores kubeadm/kubelet config in ConfigMaps
  upload-certs        (HA) shares certs with other control planes
  mark-control-plane  label + taint the node
  bootstrap-token     creates a join token
  addon               installs CoreDNS and kube-proxy
NOT installed: a CNI. You must add one, or nodes stay NotReady.


2. IMPORTANT init FLAGS
-----------------------
  --pod-network-cidr=192.168.0.0/16     must match your CNI config
  --apiserver-advertise-address=<IP>    which IP the API listens on
  --control-plane-endpoint=<LB:6443>    needed for future HA
  --kubernetes-version                  pin the version
Or use a config file: kubeadm init --config kubeadm.yaml


3. JOINING WORKERS
------------------
  kubeadm join cp1:6443 --token <t> \
    --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<hash>
The token (valid 24 h) lets the node authenticate once (TLS
bootstrap); the hash lets the node verify it's talking to the RIGHT
cluster. The kubelet then gets its own client certificate via a CSR
that is auto-approved.

New token later:
  kubeadm token create --print-join-command


4. KUBECONFIG FOR YOUR USER
---------------------------
  mkdir -p $HOME/.kube
  sudo cp /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config
  sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config
admin.conf = full admin. Protect it like a root password.


5. RESETTING
------------
  sudo kubeadm reset -f
  sudo rm -rf /etc/cni/net.d $HOME/.kube
  (and flush iptables rules) then init/join again.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- init: certs -> kubeconfigs -> static pods -> addons; no CNI.
- join uses token + CA hash.
- Nodes stay NotReady until a CNI is installed.
